«
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  @  NegBinomMu
  @  Mean of the law.
  @  Author & design          : Jean Wilson
  @  Co-authors & programming  : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
  @  Arguments may be given loose or bundled in a list of 2; that list is
  @  what LastArguments reports, and its length is checked before use.
  @ ------------------------------------------------------------
  IF DUP TypeName "list" == THEN IF DUP Size 2 == THEN Explode Drop ELSE IF DUP Size 3 == THEN Explode Drop Drop ELSE "NegBinomMu: needs 2 arguments" DoError END END END
  → rsv pv « rsv 0 + pv 0 + → rs p « 'rs*(1-p)/p' →Num rsv pv 2 →List Drop » »
»
